//! # Music System
//!
//! Reactive layered music that responds to game state.
//!
//! ## Stem Architecture
//!
//! Music is composed of synchronized stems that layer dynamically:
//!
//! ```
//! ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//! │                     MUSIC LAYERS                             │
//! ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
//! │  [Horror]   Dissonant strings, horror stingers (combat/fear)│
//! │  [Tension]  Building pads, rising pitch (danger approaching)│
//! │  [Melody]   Main theme fragments (story moments)            │
//! │  [Rhythm]   Percussion, heartbeat pulse (action/stress)     │
//! │  [Pad]      Atmospheric bed, sustained chords (always)      │
//! │  [Bass]     Low foundation (combat, tension)                │
//! └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//! ```
//!
//! ## Cue System
//!
//! Music cues define which stems play together:
//! - **Exploration**: Pad only, occasional melody fragments
//! - **Tension**: Pad + Tension, building
//! - **Combat**: Full stack (Pad + Bass + Rhythm + Horror)
//! - **Dialogue**: Pad + soft Melody, low volume
//! - **Horror**: Pad + Horror + dissonant Tension

use super::{AudioAsset, AudioChannel, AudioId};
use crate::system::PluralSystem;
use std::collections::HashMap;

